        "original_id": "89fe9c22-9347-5636-a084-135b9bb6cb77",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Dover, Strafford County, New Hampshire, United States, Seacoast Region, Rockingham County, Epping, Portsmouth\n- Concepts: regional geography, settlement history\n\nFacts:\n- The Seacoast Region in New Hampshire was the first area of the state to be permanently settled by Europeans in the early 17th century.\n- Dover is a city in Strafford County, New Hampshire, United States.\n- The Seacoast Region is the southeast area of New Hampshire that includes eastern Rockingham County and southern Strafford County.\n- The Seacoast Region extends west as far as Epping.\n- Portsmouth, the largest municipality and only city in Rockingham County, is the cultural and commercial hub of the Seacoast Region.",
